T* (Introduction) Tj
T* (AI-related technologies are developing every day, and opportunities to use AI and its) Tj
T* (various possibilities continue to expand.) Tj
T* (AI is being used to create innovation in industry and to solve social issues.) Tj
T* (With the recent rise of conversational generative AI, democratization of AI has) Tj
T* (occurred, allowing many people to easily use AI for various purposes through dialogue.) Tj
T* (As a result, companies are not only incorporating AI into business processes but are) Tj
T* (also working to reconstruct business models themselves in light of the value created by) Tj
T* (AI.) Tj
T* (Individuals are also accelerating efforts to reflect their own knowledge into AI and) Tj
T* (expand their productivity.) Tj
T* (Japan has long advocated a human-centered society that balances economic development and) Tj
T* (the solution of social issues through systems that highly integrate cyberspace and) Tj
T* (physical space as Society 5.0.) Tj
T* (To realize this concept, the Social Principles of Human-Centric AI were established in) Tj
T* (March 2019 so that AI will be accepted by society and used appropriately.) Tj
T* (As the scope of AI technology use and the number of users expand, risks are also) Tj
T* (increasing.) Tj
T* (In particular, with generative AI there are new social risks that previous AI did not) Tj
T* (pose, such as infringement of intellectual property rights and the generation and) Tj
T* (dissemination of misinformation and disinformation.) Tj
T* (The social risks brought about by AI are becoming more diverse and greater.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Against this background, these Guidelines present a unified direction for AI governance) Tj
T* (in Japan so that safe and secure use of AI will be promoted.) Tj
T* (They aim to help people who use AI in various business activities correctly recognize AI) Tj
T* (risks in light of international trends and stakeholder concerns, and to voluntarily) Tj
T* (implement necessary measures across the entire AI lifecycle.) Tj
T* (Through collaboration among related parties and through practicing common guidance and) Tj
T* (the matters important to each actor together with AI governance, the Guidelines aim to) Tj
T* (proactively co-create a framework that both promotes innovation and mitigates risks) Tj
T* (across the lifecycle.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Japan has led international discussions in forums such as the G7, G20, and OECD.) Tj
T* (At the same time, several points have been noted when advancing concrete implementation) Tj
T* (of AI principles:) Tj
T* (- AI use is expected as a means to solve social issues such as labor-force decline) Tj
T* (associated with a shrinking and aging population.) Tj
